% The Medicaid community engagement requirement (the "work requirement"),
% written in Logical English from the federal interim final rule with comment
% period of 1 June 2026, as published in the Federal Register on 3 June 2026.
%
% Source: Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services, "Medicaid Program;
% Community Engagement Requirement for Certain Individuals", interim final
% rule with comment period, 91 FR 33348 (3 June 2026), document 2026-11094,
% https://www.federalregister.gov/documents/2026/06/03/2026-11094/medicaid-program-community-engagement-requirement-for-certain-individuals
% It adds 42 CFR 435.550 to 435.563, which carry out section 1902(xx) of the
% Social Security Act, added by section 71119 of Public Law 119-21 (4 July
% 2025). Each rule below names the paragraph of 42 CFR part 435 it encodes
% and, where the preamble of the rule gives it, the subsection of section
% 1902(xx) behind it.
%
% The rule is a work of the United States federal government and is in the
% public domain. This program is provided "as is", without warranty of any
% kind. It is not legal advice and is not checked against any State's
% eligibility system.
%
% HOW IT WAS MADE. Written by hand, with an AI agent, from the regulation
% text of the rule (the amended 42 CFR part 435). The expected answers of the
% scenarios were worked out by hand from that text before the program was run
% (README.md says how).
%
% HOW TO READ IT.
% - A month is written as the date of its first day: 2027-03-01 is March 2027.
% - A case is decided at an application (the State checks 1 to 3 months
%   before the month of application) or at a renewal (the State checks 1 or
%   more months between the latest determination and the renewal).
% - The choices the rule leaves to each State are facts of a scenario: how
%   many months it checks, whether it converts income into hours of work,
%   whether it offers the short-term hardship exception, its list of
%   conditions for medical frailty, a minimum time in drug or alcohol
%   treatment, an earlier start date or a good faith exemption.
% - What the rule leaves to evidence (the hours, the income, a person's
%   status) are facts too. How a State verifies them (42 CFR 435.557) and the
%   notices it sends (435.558, 435.561) are procedure, and are not rules here,
%   except that a failed check leads to a notice of noncompliance.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base medicaid_community_engagement includes these resources:
    temporal.

the constants are:
    the federal minimum wage is 7.25.

the templates are:

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- the person and the eligibility group (435.119, 435.551)

the date of birth of *a person* is *a date*; undefined.
*a person* is eligible for the adult group; undefined.
*a person* is eligible under a demonstration that provides minimum essential coverage; undefined.
*a person* is otherwise eligible under the State plan; undefined.
*a person* is pregnant in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* is entitled to postpartum medical assistance in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* is entitled to or enrolled in Medicare in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* is described in a mandatory coverage group in *a month*; undefined.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- the decision and the State's choices (435.556, 435.559, 435.560)

*a person* applies for Medicaid in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* has a renewal due in *a month*; undefined.
the latest determination of *a person* took effect in *a month*; undefined.
the State checks *a number* months before an application; undefined.
the State checks *a number* months at a renewal; undefined.
the State implements the requirement early from *a date*; undefined.
the State has a good faith exemption until *a date*; undefined.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- activities and income in a month (435.552)

the hours of work of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the hours of community service of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the hours in a work program of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the enrolment status of *a person* in an educational program in *a month* is *a status*; undefined.
the credit hours of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the class hours of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the monthly income of *a person* in *a month* is *an amount*; undefined.
*a person* is a seasonal worker; undefined.
the State converts income into hours of work; undefined.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- the specified excluded individuals (435.554)

*a person* was in foster care and enrolled in Medicaid on turning 18; undefined.
*a person* is a member of a federally recognized tribe; undefined.
*a person* is otherwise an Indian as Medicaid cost sharing defines one; undefined.
*a person* is the legal parent of *a dependant*; undefined.
*a person* provides care to *a dependant*; undefined.
*a person* is the court appointed guardian of *a dependant*; undefined.
*a person* is a relative of *a dependant* of the kind a caretaker relative is; undefined.
*a person* lives with *a dependant*; undefined.
*a person* assumes primary responsibility for the care of *a dependant*; undefined.
*a person* has a significant relationship with *a dependant*; undefined.
*a person* gives regular assistance that is not solely incidental to *a dependant*; undefined.
the hours of assistance by *a person* to *a dependant* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
*a dependant* relies on another individual for care; undefined.
*a dependant* has a disability as the Americans with Disabilities Act defines it; undefined.
the VA disability rating of *a person* is *a number*; undefined.
*a person* has a condition that significantly impairs the ability to comply; undefined.
*a person* is blind or disabled as section 1614 defines it; undefined.
*a person* has a substance use disorder; undefined.
the years in recovery of *a person* is *a number*; undefined.
*a person* has a disabling mental disorder; undefined.
*a person* has a disability that significantly impairs an activity of daily living; undefined.
*a person* has a serious or complex medical condition; undefined.
*a person* has the diagnosis *a diagnosis*; undefined.
the State's medical frailty list includes *a diagnosis*; undefined.
*a person* complies with the TANF work requirements in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* is a member of a household that receives SNAP in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* is exempt from the SNAP work requirements in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* participates in a drug addiction or alcoholic treatment program in *a month*; undefined.
the hours of treatment of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the State's minimum hours of treatment is *a number*; undefined.
*a person* is an inmate of a public institution in *a month*; undefined.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- short-term hardship, at State option (435.555)

the State has elected the short-term hardship exception; undefined.
*a person* receives inpatient care in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* requests a hardship exception for *a month*; undefined.
*a person* resides in *a county*; undefined.
*a county* has a declared emergency or disaster in *a month*; undefined.
the unemployment rate of *a county* in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
the national unemployment rate in *a month* is *a number*; undefined.
CMS approves an unemployment hardship for *a county* in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* travels outside the community for medical treatment in *a month*; undefined.
*a dependant* is a minor child living with *a person*; undefined.
*a dependant* is a tax dependent of *a person*; undefined.
*a person* travels with *a dependant* in *a month*; undefined.
*a person* takes leave from community engagement for *a dependant* in *a month*; undefined.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------- what the rules decide

the income threshold is *an amount*.
the age of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*.
*a person* is an applicable individual in *a month*.
*a person* is subject to the requirement.
*a person* is excluded from the requirement because *a reason*.
*a person* is a specified excluded individual in *a month* because *a reason*.
*a person* is a specified excluded individual in *a month*.
*a dependant* is a dependent child in *a month*.
*a dependant* is a dependent child or a disabled individual in *a month*.
*a person* is a parent, guardian, caretaker relative or family caregiver of *a dependant* in *a month*.
*a person* is a family caregiver of *a dependant* in *a month*.
*a person* is medically frail.
*a person* meets a medical frailty category.
*a person* is in treatment for the purpose of the exclusion in *a month*.
*a person* demonstrates community engagement in *a month* because *a reason*.
*a person* engages in one qualifying activity enough in *a month*.
*a person* is enrolled at least half-time in *a month*.
the work hours counted for *a person* in *a month* is *a number*.
the community service hours counted for *a person* in *a month* is *a number*.
the work program hours counted for *a person* in *a month* is *a number*.
the education hours counted for *a person* in *a month* is *a number*.
the combined hours of *a person* in *a month* is *a number*.
the average monthly income of *a person* before *a month* is *an amount*.
*a person* is deemed to have demonstrated community engagement in *a month* because *a reason*.
*a person* was an inmate in the three months before *a month*.
*a person* has a short-term hardship in *a month* because *a reason*.
