% The State has elected the short-term hardship exception (435.555). Ola's
% county has a declared disaster; Pat's county has 7% unemployment, at least
% the lesser of 8% and 1.5 x 4.5% = 6.75%, approved by CMS; Quinn and Rae were
% in hospital, but only Rae asked for the exception, which (d)(1) requires.
scenario hardship is:
    the State checks 1 months before an application.
    the State has elected the short-term hardship exception.
    ola applies for Medicaid in 2027-03-01.
    ola is eligible for the adult group.
    the date of birth of ola is 1990-01-01.
    pat applies for Medicaid in 2027-03-01.
    pat is eligible for the adult group.
    the date of birth of pat is 1990-02-02.
    quinn applies for Medicaid in 2027-03-01.
    quinn is eligible for the adult group.
    the date of birth of quinn is 1990-03-03.
    rae applies for Medicaid in 2027-03-01.
    rae is eligible for the adult group.
    the date of birth of rae is 1990-04-04.
    ola resides in harris county.
    harris county has a declared emergency or disaster in 2027-02-01.
    pat resides in mesa county.
    CMS approves an unemployment hardship for mesa county in 2027-02-01.
    the unemployment rate of mesa county in 2027-02-01 is 7.0.
    the national unemployment rate in 2027-02-01 is 4.5.
    quinn receives inpatient care in 2027-02-01.
    rae receives inpatient care in 2027-02-01.
    rae requests a hardship exception for 2027-02-01.
    zed applies for Medicaid in 2027-03-01.
    zed is eligible for the adult group.
    the date of birth of zed is 1985-05-15.
    amy is a tax dependent of zed.
    amy travels outside the community for medical treatment in 2027-02-01.
    zed takes leave from community engagement for amy in 2027-02-01.
    zed requests a hardship exception for 2027-02-01.
    decision expects answers ["the decision for ola is meets the community engagement requirement", "the decision for pat is meets the community engagement requirement", "the decision for quinn is unable to verify: notice of noncompliance, 30 days to show compliance", "the decision for rae is meets the community engagement requirement", "the decision for zed is meets the community engagement requirement"].
    applicable expects answers ["ola is subject to the requirement", "pat is subject to the requirement", "quinn is subject to the requirement", "rae is subject to the requirement", "zed is subject to the requirement"].
    exempt expects answers [].
    meets expects answers ["ola meets the requirement in 2027-02-01", "pat meets the requirement in 2027-02-01", "rae meets the requirement in 2027-02-01", "zed meets the requirement in 2027-02-01"].
    reasons expects answers ["ola meets the requirement in 2027-02-01 because a declared emergency or disaster in the county", "pat meets the requirement in 2027-02-01 because high unemployment in the county", "rae meets the requirement in 2027-02-01 because inpatient or similar care, on request", "zed meets the requirement in 2027-02-01 because a dependant's travel for medical treatment, on request"].
